<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">scan</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">scan</ansi> command surveys the rooms adjacent to
your current location, showing you what creatures and players are nearby
without having to walk into each room.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">scan</ansi>
  Scans all visible exits and reports what you see in each
  adjacent room.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Details ━━━</ansi>

For each exit, you will see the direction, the room name, and any mobs
or players present. If a room is empty, it reports "nothing of interest."

Secret exits are not revealed by scanning.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help look</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help peek</ansi>
